id: pm-gh1603
title: "GH-1603: Reduce null agenda fields and escaped tag overhead in bounded context output"
description: "## Problem\n\n`pm context` is the first command an agent runs, and its brief depth runs under a 1,600-token budget. Two encodings in that budget carry no information:\n\n1. **Null event fields on every agenda entry.** A plain deadline entry prints 8 `event_*` keys that only calendar events use, all `null`:\n\n   ```\n   events[1]:\n     - at: \"2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z\"\n       date: 2026-11-01\n       kind: deadline\n       reminder_text: null\n       event_title: null\n       event_end: null\n       event_location: null\n       event_all_day: null\n       event_timezone: null\n       event_recurring: null\n       event_recurrence_rule: null\n       item_id: ...\n   ```\n\n   That is about 200 bytes per deadline or reminder. A tracker with 10 upcoming deadlines spends about 2 KB of a 6.4 KB brief response on nulls.\n\n2. **Tags as backslash-escaped JSON inside tabular rows.** `high_level[]` declares `json_columns: [tags]`, and each row then carries `\"[\\\"automation\\\",\\\"ci\\\",\\\"fleet\\\",\\\"release\\\"]\"`. On a real 1,300-item tracker, one `pm context --limit 10` response held 74 `\\\"` escapes, about 3% of the output, and agents have to unescape twice to read the tags.\n\n## Repro (pm-cli 2026.10.26)\n\n```bash\npm create --type Chore --title \"deadline probe\" --deadline 2026-11-01\npm context --limit 10 | grep -A12 '^  events'\npm context --limit 10 | grep -o '\\\\\"' | wc -l\n```\n\n## Proposal\n\n- Agenda entries omit `event_*` keys whose value is null (or only emit them for `kind: event`), at least at `brief` and `standard` depth. `--format json` and `--depth full` can keep the full shape for schema-stable consumers.\n- Tabular array columns use a delimiter-joined scalar that needs no escaping, declared once in the encoding header (e.g. `list_columns: {tags: \";\"}` → `automation;ci;fleet;release`). Tag values that contain the delimiter would fall back to the current JSON form.\n\nBoth changes keep the projection lossless and shrink the response that every agent session starts with.\n\n\nImplementation boundary: reproduce against the published and current hosts in an isolated tracker. Preserve SDK and full JSON data semantics, tabular codec round trips, receipts and output-budget accounting. Evaluate compact list encoding with explicit metadata and an unambiguous fallback; a delimiter proposal is not an accepted wire contract. Completed agenda deduplication and lossless JSON fixes remain delivered."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
