author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: "Native isolated deadline/reminder/event fixtures measure the actual byte and token reduction at brief and standard depth without weakening full JSON or SDK facts.; Tags round-trip through declared compact encoding with empty arrays, delimiters, commas, quotes, escapes, newlines and Unicode; ambiguous inputs retain a lossless fallback.; Serializer-aware whole-envelope budgets, omission receipts and CLI/MCP/SDK parity remain executable and unchanged."
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: medium
confidence: medium
resolution: The SDK table codec now supports safe string-list encoding and shared-null columns with explicit restoration metadata and column order. The CLI chooses the smallest complete lossless rendering; JSON and SDK facts remain unchanged.
expected_result: "Reduce context tokens without losing agenda facts, sparse keys, nulls, empty lists, escaped values, or column positions."
actual_result: "98 linked output tests pass; native deadline/reminder/scheduled-event fixtures round-trip and reduce tokens; arbitrary JSON and reserved-key cases pass; semantic negative control proves the new assertion fails when compact encoding is disabled. Typecheck and packed npx/bunx smoke pass. Exact-head hosted checks remain a required pre-merge gate; the earlier broad local run did not produce coverage after two host-sensitive failures, both passing in focused rerun."
